WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:08.739
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:51.156
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:51.282 --> 00:52.491
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.450
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.576 --> 00:54.410
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.535 --> 00:55.369
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.494 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:56.912 --> 00:58.205
[door creaks open]

10
00:59.665 --> 01:02.293
[footsteps approaching]

11
01:20.811 --> 01:23.606
I just broke up with Tae-seung and came straight here.

12
01:25.441 --> 01:27.484
I broke up with Su-a too.

13
01:32.698 --> 01:33.616
You know, right?

14
01:36.285 --> 01:38.579
That we can never go back to how we were.

15
01:41.040 --> 01:42.458
And that this is the end.

16
01:42.958 --> 01:44.877
[soft, sentimental music playing]

17
01:45.002 --> 01:46.337
It's not your fault.

18
01:48.797 --> 01:53.636
Wherever this was headed, I insisted on seeing it through.

19
01:57.222 --> 02:00.100
Even if things got ruined.

20
02:03.562 --> 02:05.439
I wanted to see it through to the end.

21
02:09.151 --> 02:10.819
It wasn't all for nothing.

22
02:14.448 --> 02:15.449
That end?

23
02:17.326 --> 02:18.410
Our rock bottom.

24
02:22.456 --> 02:24.208
Because now I know for sure…

25
02:27.753 --> 02:30.673
how terribly and also agonizingly

26
02:32.508 --> 02:33.926
we care about each other.

27
02:37.429 --> 02:39.682
I want to hurt you and ruin you more.

28
02:40.808 --> 02:42.059
And I can't, Namgung.

29
02:43.560 --> 02:44.520
It's annoying.

30
02:49.525 --> 02:50.776
[sighing] I know.

31
02:54.279 --> 02:55.406
It really is.

32
02:58.784 --> 03:00.285
Why are we such a disaster?

33
03:01.161 --> 03:02.246
What can we do?

34
03:05.666 --> 03:06.792
It's just who we are.

35
03:07.918 --> 03:09.420
[chuckles softly]

36
03:10.129 --> 03:11.296
[chuckles]

37
03:29.523 --> 03:30.566
Let's end this,

38
03:32.067 --> 03:32.901
Namgung.

39
03:35.654 --> 03:36.488
Okay.

40
03:40.951 --> 03:41.785
Let's end this.

41
03:46.957 --> 03:47.958
Let's end this,

42
03:49.418 --> 03:50.419
Mi-do.

43
03:50.544 --> 03:52.004
[music swells]

44
04:02.097 --> 04:06.060
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

45
04:06.185 --> 04:12.066
WHAT BROUGHT US TOGETHER?

46
04:12.191 --> 04:13.692
[soft, sentimental music concludes]

47
04:13.817 --> 04:16.028
[door keypad beeping]

48
04:19.239 --> 04:20.449
[door lock chimes]

49
04:29.416 --> 04:30.626
[door lock chimes]

50
04:46.183 --> 04:47.267
[groans softly]

51
04:50.020 --> 04:51.897
[Mi-do] Namgung did nothing wrong.

52
04:54.650 --> 04:57.611
I fell for another man, and that's why we broke up.

53
05:01.240 --> 05:03.158
So Mom, just treat him like before.

54
05:03.283 --> 05:05.661
I've never seen Hoya cry like that.

55
05:08.372 --> 05:10.666
He was crying his heart out.

56
05:11.500 --> 05:14.837
He cried for hours, and before leaving, he didn't say anything.

57
05:16.588 --> 05:19.925
I don't know what happened or why you two decided to break up,

58
05:20.717 --> 05:24.596
but I know you'll never get back together.

59
05:24.847 --> 05:26.431
I feel it in my old bones.

60
05:27.683 --> 05:28.934
[gentle music playing]

61
05:29.059 --> 05:34.940
I no longer remember your dad's face when I see a photo of him.

62
05:37.860 --> 05:41.822
I always think, "Oh, that's what he looked like."

63
05:42.739 --> 05:44.449
That's how he used to smile.

64
05:44.908 --> 05:46.702
And it stings a little inside.

65
05:47.619 --> 05:50.330
But that's the extent of it.

66
05:54.042 --> 06:00.340
As life goes on, life gets so busy that it fades away.

67
06:01.925 --> 06:03.051
It all disappears.

68
06:04.928 --> 06:08.348
You wonder how something like that can occur.

69
06:10.184 --> 06:14.229
And then comes a day when that feels so sad.

70
06:15.731 --> 06:17.482
You too will be that way too.

71
06:18.901 --> 06:23.155
So don't hate or resent him and don't hold grudges.

72
06:23.530 --> 06:25.741
Don't struggle so hard to forget him.

73
06:27.367 --> 06:28.869
Just let it all flow.

74
06:30.370 --> 06:32.039
If you just let it be…

75
06:34.333 --> 06:35.375
you'll be okay.

76
06:38.462 --> 06:39.546
You will move on.

77
06:43.675 --> 06:45.177
[exhales deeply]

78
06:49.264 --> 06:50.390
[gentle music concludes]

79
06:50.515 --> 06:53.310
BORA BORA ROOM HONDURAS

80
07:10.285 --> 07:11.370
[sighs]

81
07:13.121 --> 07:17.793
[melody tinkling softly over music box]

82
07:24.383 --> 07:27.552
[Bo-ra] Sorry, I didn't think you'd find it this late.

83
07:27.678 --> 07:28.845
[melody concludes]

84
07:32.474 --> 07:38.438
I thought that once I died, you'd get rid of this place first.

85
07:41.316 --> 07:42.526
I could never do that.

86
07:44.945 --> 07:47.906
Honduras is the only thing you left behind for me.

87
07:49.408 --> 07:50.575
How could I ever leave?

88
07:58.333 --> 07:59.293
Bo-ra.

89
08:00.252 --> 08:01.295
Hmm?

90
08:01.878 --> 08:02.921
I…

91
08:05.757 --> 08:07.426
I really loved you, you know?

92
08:10.387 --> 08:12.180
It's true, I was exhausted.

93
08:13.682 --> 08:15.892
And I hurt you because of that, really.

94
08:18.979 --> 08:19.855
But even so…

95
08:23.442 --> 08:25.027
I loved you with all my heart.

96
08:28.488 --> 08:29.323
I know.

97
08:30.991 --> 08:31.825
You do?

98
08:33.660 --> 08:34.995
[tender music playing]

99
08:36.038 --> 08:37.205
[Bo-ra sobs softly]

100
08:42.294 --> 08:43.128
Wan-do?

101
08:44.713 --> 08:45.630
Hmm?

102
08:47.799 --> 08:52.554
The beach in Bora Bora, do you remember that we promised to go together?

103
08:55.015 --> 08:55.849
[Wan-do] Mm-hmm.

104
08:56.141 --> 08:57.601
I want to go there with you.

105
09:05.776 --> 09:06.860
Can you take me there?

106
09:10.906 --> 09:14.534
[melody tinkling softly over music box]

107
09:16.119 --> 09:17.162
[melody concludes]

108
09:24.044 --> 09:25.837
[sobbing softly]

109
09:25.962 --> 09:27.714
[tender music continues]

110
09:28.632 --> 09:29.925
These don't look good either.

111
09:30.550 --> 09:32.928
Flashy things don't suit me anymore.

112
09:34.971 --> 09:36.390
[Sang-su] Of course they do.

113
09:36.807 --> 09:38.350
You look gorgeous, Mom.

114
09:39.434 --> 09:40.477
Beautiful.

115
09:44.439 --> 09:46.024
[groans] Father made me do it.

116
09:46.525 --> 09:48.110
To say you're pretty 12 times.

117
09:48.693 --> 09:50.445
And that you look younger than your fiancé.

118
09:51.238 --> 09:53.073
I'll tell your dad you were here for an hour.

119
09:56.284 --> 09:58.203
Why? Something to say?

120
10:00.664 --> 10:01.498
Need allowance?

121
10:01.623 --> 10:02.666
Uh…

122
10:04.584 --> 10:06.128
I'll never call him Father.

123
10:06.670 --> 10:08.338
He didn't expect you to.

124
10:09.464 --> 10:10.382
Congratulations.

125
10:12.551 --> 10:14.344
Dad might need some time to mean it.

126
10:15.387 --> 10:16.805
Still, I mean every word.

127
10:17.597 --> 10:19.433
And please understand Dad.

128
10:20.851 --> 10:21.685
Okay.

129
10:29.860 --> 10:31.778
He really kept that promise.

130
10:35.907 --> 10:37.325
[tender music concludes]

131
10:39.995 --> 10:41.246
[upbeat music playing over speakers]

132
10:41.371 --> 10:42.539
Yeah.

133
10:42.914 --> 10:44.249
Oh, you're such a cutie.

134
10:45.542 --> 10:46.960
I said to get ox bone soup.

135
10:47.085 --> 10:48.211
You know Sang-su loves that.

136
10:49.546 --> 10:50.505
It's good.

137
10:50.630 --> 10:51.756
Here, a bite.

138
10:52.007 --> 10:54.176
Ah!

139
10:55.177 --> 10:56.136
Yes.

140
10:56.803 --> 10:58.388
I like burgers too.

141
10:58.847 --> 10:59.890
Here. Oh.

142
11:00.182 --> 11:01.224
You love it?

143
11:01.641 --> 11:02.601
Ketchup, huh?

144
11:03.852 --> 11:04.853
I forgot it.

145
11:05.687 --> 11:06.980
It's bad for him anyway.

146
11:07.105 --> 11:07.939
Just eat.

147
11:12.486 --> 11:13.695
[burger squelches]

148
11:18.825 --> 11:20.368
Can't you just please reconsider?

149
11:20.869 --> 11:21.745
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

150
11:21.870 --> 11:22.787
Just one last time.

151
11:22.913 --> 11:24.247
I… [hesitates]

152
11:24.372 --> 11:26.333
I just feel so bad for Sang-su, you know?

153
11:27.334 --> 11:30.378
Even if you're not my wife, can't you stay as Sang-su's mom?

154
11:31.171 --> 11:32.797
I'm begging you, please just do it for him!

155
11:36.301 --> 11:37.135
You…

156
11:39.012 --> 11:40.680
don't really need me.

157
11:42.933 --> 11:44.392
[somber music playing]

158
11:51.274 --> 11:53.068
[Mun-yeong] Never let him find out.

159
11:54.444 --> 11:56.780
You were so pathetic back then.

160
11:59.074 --> 12:00.909
So pathetic it hurts.

161
12:11.378 --> 12:13.004
YEONHWARU

162
12:13.129 --> 12:15.173
[exhales deeply]

163
12:18.593 --> 12:19.594
[Namgung] Excuse me.

164
12:23.598 --> 12:26.476
It's… It's my first time here.

165
12:27.602 --> 12:28.895
What's good here?

166
12:45.704 --> 12:49.833
[crying]

167
12:53.211 --> 12:56.923
NAMGUNG, MI-DO

168
13:02.137 --> 13:04.973
[Mi-do sobbing]

169
13:07.309 --> 13:08.518
[somber music concludes]

170
13:08.643 --> 13:10.770
[announcement chimes]

171
13:10.895 --> 13:13.315
2 YEARS LATER

172
13:13.481 --> 13:17.360
[passenger yawning]

173
13:17.777 --> 13:23.116
I NEVER RESIGNED BY EOM HO-SIK

174
13:29.998 --> 13:31.625
[passenger] Oh, thank you.

175
13:34.711 --> 13:36.755
[announcer] Now boarding for Flight…

176
13:43.762 --> 13:45.513
SPICY SWEETATO CHIPS HO-SIK'S PICK

177
13:49.059 --> 13:51.061
[bold, exciting music playing]

178
13:51.895 --> 13:52.937
[scoffs]

179
13:53.938 --> 13:55.815
Executive Director Yoon is up to something.

180
13:56.650 --> 13:58.610
He's been calling in the executives privately.

181
13:59.277 --> 14:02.322
And now he's eyeing a restructuring.

182
14:03.990 --> 14:06.034
I need you to take over that team.

183
14:06.826 --> 14:07.786
You will be the team leader.

184
14:08.203 --> 14:09.162
A 20% raise.

185
14:09.579 --> 14:10.497
Huh?

186
14:10.622 --> 14:14.125
And I also want a separate bonus contract of up to 20%

187
14:14.250 --> 14:15.835
based on project KPIs.

188
14:16.544 --> 14:18.046
Then I'll be giving it some thought.

189
14:18.171 --> 14:20.048
Like hell you will, dammit!

190
14:20.173 --> 14:22.467
I'm being ground down at work and it's because of you!

191
14:22.592 --> 14:25.303
Listen, if only you hadn't posted that video!

192
14:25.428 --> 14:27.222
[groans wearily] Seriously!

193
14:27.972 --> 14:28.973
[employee 1] Did you see this?

194
14:30.475 --> 14:31.434
Lookie here.

195
14:32.143 --> 14:32.977
[employee 2] What's this?

196
14:34.479 --> 14:35.939
SWEET POTATO SWAP

197
14:36.106 --> 14:37.232
Oh, wait a sec.

198
14:38.483 --> 14:39.984
[employee 3] Is that our manager?

199
14:40.110 --> 14:41.695
-It is, right? -[employee 2 gasps] Yeah, it's him.

200
14:41.820 --> 14:42.946
[employee 1] Right, that's Manager Eom.

201
14:43.071 --> 14:44.864
-See, told you. -[employee 2] It is.

202
14:45.615 --> 14:48.034
-[employee 4] Oh, hey, this dropped. -[driver] Yes, sir.

203
14:48.159 --> 14:51.079
SWEET POTATOES

204
14:51.204 --> 14:53.081
[employee 4] Please, don't damage them.

205
14:56.334 --> 14:57.961
HM CONFECTIONERY EXPOSED!

206
15:00.505 --> 15:01.923
OVER 5 MILLION VIEWS

207
15:02.257 --> 15:03.341
HERO EOM HO-SIK TRUE MENTOR EOM

208
15:03.466 --> 15:04.426
I LOVE HIM

209
15:04.551 --> 15:06.136
I NEVER RESIGNED BY EOM HO-SIK

210
15:06.678 --> 15:08.263
TRULY INSPIRING A PAGE-TURNER

211
15:08.638 --> 15:10.348
SWEET, SPICY, AND ADDICTIVE

212
15:10.473 --> 15:12.100
DIRECTOR EOM HO-SIK

213
15:12.225 --> 15:13.768
-[bold, exciting music concludes] -Hey, Namgung.

214
15:13.893 --> 15:15.311
This isn't the life I wanted.

215
15:15.437 --> 15:17.230
I wanted to go to Tongyeong, hmm?

216
15:17.355 --> 15:18.815
Collect my paychecks month after month.

217
15:18.940 --> 15:21.443
That's all I wanted. Now look at this mess, hmm?

218
15:21.568 --> 15:23.570
I'm caught in this bloody power struggle.

219
15:23.695 --> 15:25.488
Oh, it's suffocating.

220
15:25.613 --> 15:26.865
I'm choking!

221
15:27.657 --> 15:28.783
Goodness sake.

222
15:28.908 --> 15:31.119
I never wanted to climb this high, huh?

223
15:31.369 --> 15:32.203
Eom, hey.

224
15:33.288 --> 15:34.748
Why are you being so weak?

225
15:35.039 --> 15:36.541
Gen Z will be disappointed.

226
15:37.208 --> 15:38.418
Dammit, I don't care.

227
15:38.543 --> 15:39.919
I'm not going to suffer alone.

228
15:40.044 --> 15:40.920
You are too.

229
15:41.045 --> 15:41.963
We're both on this.

230
15:42.088 --> 15:43.339
We're meant to get crushed.

231
15:43.673 --> 15:44.632
Now come back to work!

232
15:45.216 --> 15:46.468
Let's talk salary first.

233
15:46.593 --> 15:48.428
-You punk! -[footsteps approaching rapidly]

234
15:50.513 --> 15:52.974
[panting]

235
15:56.269 --> 15:57.187
Oh, Ms. Park.

236
15:58.605 --> 15:59.481
We were…

237
16:00.190 --> 16:02.942
Mr. Namgung will start working at headquarters.

238
16:03.610 --> 16:04.444
Next week.

239
16:06.696 --> 16:09.324
You two haven't seen each other in two years.

240
16:12.410 --> 16:14.204
Long time no see, Su-a. Hi.

241
16:16.247 --> 16:17.081
Or…

242
16:18.958 --> 16:19.959
Senior Associate Park.

243
16:25.048 --> 16:26.090
The Mason Project.

244
16:27.050 --> 16:28.635
You rejected the vendor we found.

245
16:28.760 --> 16:29.594
May I ask why?

246
16:30.345 --> 16:33.765
Ah, Louis Maltese, the pastry guy or whatever?

247
16:33.890 --> 16:35.391
Louis Martin, the pastry chef.

248
16:36.309 --> 16:38.019
The top pastry chef in Paris.

249
16:39.020 --> 16:41.856
We just needed sign-off after working hard to contact him.

250
16:41.981 --> 16:43.066
Why did you reject it?

251
16:43.608 --> 16:44.734
I didn't like his face.

252
16:45.360 --> 16:46.361
[scoffs]

253
16:46.486 --> 16:47.821
[light music playing]

254
16:48.655 --> 16:49.781
I'm just kidding.

255
16:52.033 --> 16:53.576
Come to my party to find out.

256
17:03.670 --> 17:04.796
I can't make it today.

257
17:05.547 --> 17:06.589
I have a blind date.

258
17:06.714 --> 17:07.757
And I didn't ask.

259
17:09.217 --> 17:13.721
Ms. Park, in situations like this, just say you have personal plans.

260
17:13.847 --> 17:16.850
You got promoted a while ago, but you still lack tact.

261
17:17.725 --> 17:18.768
I'll hear your reasons.

262
17:19.269 --> 17:21.145
In person when you come in next week.

263
17:32.574 --> 17:35.034
Defendant Sim Hae-ju is a repeat offender

264
17:35.159 --> 17:36.411
with a criminal record

265
17:37.370 --> 17:40.206
who has engaged in illegal hacking since his teens.

266
17:42.375 --> 17:44.502
The defendant is not a mere hacker.

267
17:44.878 --> 17:48.131
Plus, per the client's request, he illegally obtained…

268
17:48.256 --> 17:49.257
THE WORST WOMAN

269
17:49.465 --> 17:50.925
[Tae-seung] Start getting ready to cry.

270
17:51.050 --> 17:53.177
[prosecutor] …acting as a broker for financial gain.

271
17:53.303 --> 17:55.054
Should a defense lawyer say that?

272
17:55.179 --> 17:57.682
To get at least six months off, you'd better cry.

273
17:58.349 --> 18:00.643
A single tear gets you six months off.

274
18:01.019 --> 18:03.271
Bawling your eyes out gets you a year.

275
18:03.563 --> 18:04.981
Why did you even take my case?

276
18:05.106 --> 18:06.774
DEFENSE, DEFENDANT

277
18:06.900 --> 18:09.235
You knew who I was from the start.

278
18:10.153 --> 18:10.987
[judge] Please continue.

279
18:11.613 --> 18:14.657
[prosecutor] In particular, the defendant obtained targets' identities

280
18:14.782 --> 18:15.700
and daily routines…

281
18:15.825 --> 18:18.202
The woman I like told me to be good.

282
18:18.870 --> 18:20.914
So I do pro bono work every now and then.

283
18:22.248 --> 18:23.833
And you looked so pathetic.

284
18:24.709 --> 18:25.627
So why not?

285
18:25.752 --> 18:28.129
[prosecutor] …delivering that information to his clients in exchange…

286
18:28.254 --> 18:29.797
-[scoffs] -[mid-tempo music playing]

287
18:30.381 --> 18:31.591
He's wrapping it up.

288
18:31.883 --> 18:33.176
Start crying now.

289
18:33.718 --> 18:38.431
[prosecutor continues indistinctly]

290
18:38.556 --> 18:40.516
Think back to when your grandma died.

291
18:40.934 --> 18:41.768
Hey, man, what…

292
18:42.226 --> 18:46.105
Or back in middle school, when you got expelled.

293
18:47.857 --> 18:49.943
You used to live in Seoul Station, right?

294
18:50.693 --> 18:51.527
Yes.

295
18:52.362 --> 18:53.947
But… But that's irrelevant.

296
18:55.782 --> 18:57.867
Well, if I had met you way back then…

297
19:02.538 --> 19:05.583
I'd have made sure you weren't unfairly expelled.

298
19:06.626 --> 19:11.047
And given your grandma a proper funeral instead of that horrible thing she had.

299
19:13.841 --> 19:15.760
And you getting beaten by homeless guys.

300
19:17.220 --> 19:18.846
None of that would have happened.

301
19:20.890 --> 19:22.934
-[prosecutor] We have not reached… -[sobbing softly]

302
19:27.105 --> 19:27.939
Well done.

303
19:29.482 --> 19:30.733
Now don't stop.

304
19:30.858 --> 19:33.403
[prosecutor] …that the defendant be sentenced to five years.

305
19:33.528 --> 19:36.531
[sobbing]

306
19:37.490 --> 19:39.784
[judge] Counsel, your closing argument.

307
19:41.869 --> 19:43.788
The prosecution's claims are false.

308
19:44.580 --> 19:46.791
[Mi-do] Where would you make the cut here?

309
19:46.916 --> 19:48.918
FILM DIRECTING

310
19:49.085 --> 19:51.587
The right answer doesn't exist.

311
19:52.630 --> 19:55.717
Nevertheless, you have to be able to explain why you cut it here.

312
19:57.427 --> 19:59.012
Directing isn't about the right answers.

313
19:59.137 --> 20:01.055
It's about making choices

314
20:01.180 --> 20:03.891
and convincing people of your choices to the end.

315
20:05.268 --> 20:06.894
Now, let's see the next scene.

316
20:08.396 --> 20:10.064
[students chattering]

317
20:14.777 --> 20:16.029
Good work, everyone.

318
20:16.154 --> 20:17.655
GIMUN UNIVERSITY

319
20:19.991 --> 20:22.910
[Wan-do] Listen, I didn't know if I should tell you,

320
20:23.036 --> 20:24.704
but you should probably know.

321
20:25.872 --> 20:26.873
Namgung is back.

322
20:27.707 --> 20:30.585
So please, don't come home for a while.

323
20:31.335 --> 20:32.879
What if he doesn't visit because he…

324
20:33.004 --> 20:34.505
-[exhales deeply] -[mid-tempo music concludes]

325
20:34.630 --> 20:36.090
[student 1] What is he even saying?

326
20:36.215 --> 20:38.801
[student 2] Hey, did you hear about the equipment office?

327
20:39.886 --> 20:41.054
[student 3] Is it true?

328
20:41.554 --> 20:43.473
They said an FX7 got totally wrecked.

329
20:43.848 --> 20:46.017
Isn't that at least ten million won?

330
20:46.350 --> 20:48.478
The chair is desperate to catch who did it.

331
20:48.895 --> 20:51.105
Apparently, the security cameras on that floor

332
20:51.230 --> 20:52.398
and throughout the building…

333
20:52.899 --> 20:54.067
Bam, they were down.

334
20:54.567 --> 20:57.236
[student 3] But the TA said he saw a man and a woman go

335
20:57.361 --> 20:58.988
in there right at that time, right?

336
21:00.448 --> 21:01.616
Together they stayed there.

337
21:02.241 --> 21:03.409
Wait, both of them in there?

338
21:03.701 --> 21:04.577
[student 3] Yes.

339
21:04.702 --> 21:06.579
[student 2] Damn, what were they doing in there?

340
21:06.704 --> 21:08.081
[student 3] What else? It's obvious.

341
21:08.206 --> 21:10.333
-[student 2] That's crazy. -[student 3] Come on, let's get coffee.

342
21:10.458 --> 21:11.918
[perky music playing]

343
21:17.090 --> 21:20.051
FILM EQUIPMENT OFFICE

344
21:39.362 --> 21:40.446
[Tae-seung] Looking for this?

345
21:42.198 --> 21:43.032
[Mi-do] What?

346
21:43.491 --> 21:44.575
How'd you get in here?

347
21:46.160 --> 21:47.370
Same way as last time.

348
21:48.246 --> 21:49.247
[sighs]

349
21:51.332 --> 21:52.166
Just kidding.

350
21:55.336 --> 21:56.587
I have two card cases.

351
21:58.798 --> 21:59.632
What?

352
22:00.091 --> 22:00.925
So you didn't find it?

353
22:01.968 --> 22:02.802
Nope.

354
22:02.927 --> 22:03.970
[sighs]

355
22:05.596 --> 22:07.014
And mine wasn't the only card in there.

356
22:07.140 --> 22:07.974
Don't worry.

357
22:08.349 --> 22:09.809
I took care of the cameras, too.

358
22:09.934 --> 22:12.520
-Still, just in case, I'd feel better if-- -[Tae-seung] Namgung.

359
22:13.896 --> 22:14.939
I heard he came back.

360
22:15.648 --> 22:16.858
[perky music concludes]

361
22:20.736 --> 22:21.821
So you already knew.

362
22:26.200 --> 22:27.368
You went back to my mom?

363
22:27.493 --> 22:28.703
For a root touch-up.

364
22:28.828 --> 22:30.830
Who gets their roots touched up every week?

365
22:31.330 --> 22:32.331
Forget it.

366
22:32.957 --> 22:33.791
Don't go anymore.

367
22:34.375 --> 22:35.293
I'm warning you.

368
22:35.710 --> 22:36.544
Why?

369
22:37.420 --> 22:39.005
Worried I'll run into Namgung there?

370
22:42.800 --> 22:43.759
[scoffs]

371
22:47.180 --> 22:48.264
Do you miss him?

372
22:54.020 --> 22:55.313
Do you miss Namgung?

373
22:56.772 --> 22:57.732
Answer me.

374
23:05.531 --> 23:06.908
[student 3] You sure you left it in here?

375
23:07.033 --> 23:09.619
[student 1] Uh, I don't remember, but I was definitely in here.

376
23:10.369 --> 23:11.454
[student 2] You don't remember?

377
23:11.579 --> 23:13.080
-[student 2] Stop losing it. -Seriously?

378
23:13.206 --> 23:14.790
-Oh, jeez. -Did you check inside?

379
23:14.916 --> 23:15.791
Here it is.

380
23:15.917 --> 23:16.751
I thought I lost it.

381
23:17.335 --> 23:18.544
-You're so clumsy. -Cut it out.

382
23:18.669 --> 23:19.712
Cut it out now, please.

383
23:19.837 --> 23:21.964
-You're a pain. -[student 3] Iced coffee. Go.

384
23:31.974 --> 23:33.267
Were you playing with me?

385
23:36.520 --> 23:40.233
You can play with me, but only with me, Mi-do.

386
23:41.984 --> 23:42.985
[exhales softly]

387
23:43.778 --> 23:44.654
[Tae-seung] Fine.

388
23:44.779 --> 23:45.988
I admit I was clingy.

389
23:47.240 --> 23:51.160
However, you indulged me one out of ten times.

390
23:51.911 --> 23:52.912
You gave me hope.

391
23:53.788 --> 23:54.997
You didn't pull away just now.

392
23:56.165 --> 23:57.166
You made my heart race.

393
23:58.709 --> 24:00.711
[tender music playing]

394
24:09.553 --> 24:10.596
Tell me you don't.

395
24:13.683 --> 24:17.812
Tell me you don't miss Namgung at all.

396
24:22.149 --> 24:23.609
Are you really that paranoid?

397
24:26.487 --> 24:28.489
Do you still think I'm playing with you?

398
24:31.951 --> 24:33.160
[inhales deeply]

399
24:33.286 --> 24:35.162
You asked if I miss Namgung.

400
24:36.330 --> 24:37.540
Hmm. I do.

401
24:37.665 --> 24:38.666
I miss him.

402
24:40.251 --> 24:41.669
But not in the way that you think.

403
24:43.170 --> 24:47.508
I just… wonder how he's doing.

404
24:48.759 --> 24:49.593
I'm just worried.

405
24:52.972 --> 24:53.848
Also…

406
24:58.102 --> 25:01.230
it hurts so much to see you getting hurt because of me.

407
25:03.691 --> 25:05.568
Seeing you suffer because of Namgung…

408
25:07.945 --> 25:09.030
breaks my heart.

409
25:13.242 --> 25:15.703
So I can't let myself follow my heart to you.

410
25:25.212 --> 25:27.381
You think I'm hurting because of Namgung?

411
25:34.305 --> 25:35.139
No.

412
25:36.766 --> 25:38.642
It's because you won't give me an answer.

413
25:41.687 --> 25:42.855
Just do it.

414
25:44.023 --> 25:48.110
If you don't want to hurt me, give me an answer.

415
26:45.626 --> 26:47.002
[tender music concludes]

416
26:50.005 --> 26:51.507
How was your blind date?

417
26:58.722 --> 27:00.391
[door keypad beeping]

418
27:05.479 --> 27:06.439
[door lock chimes]

419
27:09.525 --> 27:10.693
[sighs]

420
27:19.702 --> 27:20.619
I have a question.

421
27:22.037 --> 27:22.872
Go ahead.

422
27:23.330 --> 27:26.083
Why did you send me those plants?

423
27:27.084 --> 27:29.044
My transfer at the beginning of the year

424
27:29.795 --> 27:34.133
got canceled when the Mason Project went with local collaboration.

425
27:35.801 --> 27:37.261
But I'd already shipped my things.

426
27:39.346 --> 27:42.308
And plant quarantine is strict, so I couldn't get them back.

427
27:43.267 --> 27:44.101
I liked them.

428
27:45.644 --> 27:48.105
So I wondered who'd take the best care of them.

429
27:49.398 --> 27:50.274
So I chose you.

430
27:51.942 --> 27:52.776
That's a lie.

431
27:53.611 --> 27:54.445
Your transfer.

432
27:55.654 --> 27:56.989
You canceled it yourself.

433
27:57.615 --> 28:00.618
The team had been assembled, but you just canceled it.

434
28:01.619 --> 28:02.995
It was originally six months,

435
28:03.120 --> 28:05.247
but you stayed two years because you wanted to.

436
28:07.875 --> 28:09.001
Was it because of Mi-do?

437
28:12.087 --> 28:13.589
You stayed away because of Mi-do.

438
28:17.676 --> 28:19.261
Do you think it was because of her?

439
28:19.386 --> 28:20.221
Was it not?

440
28:20.638 --> 28:21.472
It wasn't.

441
28:22.973 --> 28:24.266
I just thought that

442
28:25.726 --> 28:27.811
my feelings for you had to be 100%.

443
28:29.647 --> 28:32.024
And until then, I shouldn't return here.

444
28:45.246 --> 28:46.539
What do you feel now?

445
28:48.832 --> 28:50.000
Do you love me now?

446
28:53.045 --> 28:54.171
Is that why you came back?

447
28:57.258 --> 28:58.092
No.

448
29:02.137 --> 29:03.722
I couldn't make it zero percent.

449
29:06.517 --> 29:07.893
[sweet music playing]

450
29:08.352 --> 29:09.603
That's why I returned.

451
29:23.909 --> 29:25.369
[Su-a] Who was that woman?

452
29:25.494 --> 29:28.789
You were eating gelato with her back in April.

453
29:29.498 --> 29:31.333
Mr. Oh said he saw you.

454
29:32.042 --> 29:33.544
My neighbor, Juliette Laurent.

455
29:34.003 --> 29:34.837
What are you two?

456
29:35.129 --> 29:36.380
We eat gelato together.

457
29:38.090 --> 29:41.927
For the record, her girlfriend is in our Paris team, Camille.

458
29:44.805 --> 29:45.639
Anything else?

459
29:45.764 --> 29:46.599
Nothing.

460
30:00.362 --> 30:01.447
Martin, the pasty chef.

461
30:02.072 --> 30:03.324
Why did you reject him?

462
30:04.450 --> 30:05.326
Seriously, right now?

463
30:05.451 --> 30:06.535
Because Lumière Homme

464
30:06.994 --> 30:09.121
named him one of the most attractive men in their thirties.

465
30:10.748 --> 30:11.790
Am I right?

466
30:13.667 --> 30:15.127
Not because of another issue.

467
30:15.919 --> 30:17.546
You didn't want me working with him.

468
30:18.505 --> 30:19.340
You were jealous.

469
30:20.507 --> 30:21.467
Am I right?

470
30:28.641 --> 30:29.642
Hey.

471
30:29.767 --> 30:30.726
Why did you kill it?

472
30:31.727 --> 30:33.729
The snake plant I gave you before you left.

473
30:34.480 --> 30:36.231
Why did you kill just that plant?

474
30:44.573 --> 30:45.949
It's because of you.

475
30:46.742 --> 30:48.827
You said to water it when I missed you.

476
30:49.370 --> 30:50.704
And I did, so it died.

477
30:54.625 --> 30:55.709
You have more questions?

478
30:57.586 --> 30:58.420
That's it.

479
30:58.796 --> 30:59.630
No, no, no.

480
31:00.005 --> 31:01.048
You said that earlier.

481
31:01.423 --> 31:02.257
Think carefully.

482
31:02.800 --> 31:04.134
There might be more.

483
31:16.146 --> 31:17.106
I missed you.

484
31:19.900 --> 31:21.944
I missed you very much, Namgung.

485
31:45.050 --> 31:46.427
[sweet music concludes]

486
31:52.850 --> 31:54.852
Has it been six months already?

487
31:55.477 --> 31:58.647
Now that that punk Namgung is back, we can go float fishing.

488
31:59.773 --> 32:01.942
Great. No weekend classes this term.

489
32:02.401 --> 32:03.736
Oh, really? That's great.

490
32:04.862 --> 32:07.489
You two, I need you to bring this food over to Hoya, please.

491
32:09.491 --> 32:11.118
He's coming tomorrow evening.

492
32:17.708 --> 32:20.085
-Bro! -Hey, what did you just say?

493
32:20.627 --> 32:22.004
You can't call anyone, no texts.

494
32:22.463 --> 32:23.714
And don't send messages.

495
32:25.674 --> 32:28.218
We'll meet here once a year on Wan-do's birthday.

496
32:36.643 --> 32:38.979
From now on, let's just meet yearly, okay?

497
32:43.776 --> 32:46.612
BROTHER CLEANING

498
33:03.962 --> 33:05.422
This is about what happened, right?

499
33:06.965 --> 33:08.383
Because of what I said then?

500
33:10.803 --> 33:12.471
You know that's not why, Yeong-do.

501
33:16.517 --> 33:19.144
Even if you set Mi-do aside, what about Mom?

502
33:21.146 --> 33:22.189
What about that Wan-do?

503
33:25.234 --> 33:26.360
Don't you worry about us at all?

504
33:26.777 --> 33:27.611
No, I don't.

505
33:30.948 --> 33:32.491
Because I know you'll be okay.

506
33:35.494 --> 33:37.371
You'll look after them better than anyone.

507
33:39.915 --> 33:41.124
So I'm not worried at all.

508
33:43.669 --> 33:44.962
[gentle guitar music playing]

509
33:55.639 --> 33:56.640
Of course, that's a given.

510
33:57.641 --> 33:59.434
I'm the eldest son of our clan, Namgung.

511
34:00.686 --> 34:02.104
Who'll look after us if not me?

512
34:02.479 --> 34:04.064
Of course I will always look after us.

513
34:09.152 --> 34:09.987
I'll take care of you,

514
34:11.029 --> 34:11.905
Namgung.

515
34:13.240 --> 34:14.366
I'll take care of you too.

516
34:16.201 --> 34:17.035
Of course I will.

517
34:18.161 --> 34:19.246
You're my brother.

518
34:21.832 --> 34:24.042
You're my brother even if I see you once a year.

519
34:26.044 --> 34:29.214
Once a brother, you are always a brother.

520
34:31.049 --> 34:31.884
Got it?

521
34:34.177 --> 34:35.012
Got it?

522
34:37.806 --> 34:38.932
Say you got it.

523
34:45.814 --> 34:47.316
Why don't you say it?

524
34:50.485 --> 34:52.738
Say something. [sobs softly]

525
34:54.740 --> 34:55.782
Why don't you say it?

526
34:59.036 --> 34:59.953
[sobs]

527
35:06.335 --> 35:07.669
[gentle guitar music concludes]

528
35:15.844 --> 35:16.678
[sighs]

529
35:23.185 --> 35:26.271
We'll still meet once a year, so don't be too upset, please.

530
35:29.900 --> 35:31.068
How are your classes going?

531
35:32.444 --> 35:33.278
Still lifting weights?

532
35:34.237 --> 35:35.072
Hey.

533
35:36.281 --> 35:37.908
Sometimes they catch huge fish here.

534
35:41.662 --> 35:44.247
Is once every five years really sometimes?

535
35:45.958 --> 35:47.250
[scoffs] It's the owner's gimmick.

536
35:48.669 --> 35:49.711
It'll grant you a wish

537
35:51.088 --> 35:52.130
if you release it.

538
35:53.173 --> 35:54.007
Doesn't matter.

539
35:54.925 --> 35:57.970
Even if the fish grants you a wish, it's once a year.

540
35:59.137 --> 35:59.972
No more often than that.

541
36:02.432 --> 36:03.892
I think that in the next life…

542
36:06.812 --> 36:08.313
I will be born as your dad.

543
36:12.025 --> 36:13.568
[tender Korean pop song playing]

544
36:14.903 --> 36:15.737
I really will.

545
36:18.073 --> 36:18.907
In this life…

546
36:21.702 --> 36:22.953
we could end things here.

547
36:25.247 --> 36:29.251
But in the next one, I promise I'll be your dad.

548
36:32.129 --> 36:36.383
So that I can repay everything…

549
36:39.177 --> 36:40.345
you've done for me…

550
36:42.973 --> 36:43.890
many times over.

551
36:45.225 --> 36:46.351
[exhales deeply]

552
36:47.978 --> 36:48.854
[sniffles]

553
36:56.570 --> 36:57.654
[sniffles]

554
37:02.034 --> 37:02.951
Hey.

555
37:09.041 --> 37:12.461
[crying softly]

556
37:14.838 --> 37:16.089
You'll do just fine.

557
37:19.968 --> 37:20.927
Even without us,

558
37:23.221 --> 37:24.139
you'll do really well.

559
37:29.436 --> 37:30.520
Thank you.

560
38:39.589 --> 38:41.007
[tender Korean pop song concludes]

561
38:41.133 --> 38:42.300
This wasn't a coincidence.

562
38:47.013 --> 38:48.932
I waited over two hours downstairs,

563
38:50.934 --> 38:53.270
which means I could easily avoid you too.

564
38:55.355 --> 38:56.773
Even if you visit my family,

565
38:58.275 --> 39:00.026
we will never cross paths again.

566
39:03.947 --> 39:05.031
I heard from Yeong-do.

567
39:06.199 --> 39:08.201
You said you'd see my family only once a year, Namgung.

568
39:11.454 --> 39:12.289
Please don't bother.

569
39:13.915 --> 39:15.375
We were fine for two years.

570
39:17.627 --> 39:19.713
-So please, let's just continue-- -I put it off.

571
39:23.383 --> 39:24.759
I needed some time, Mi-do.

572
39:27.971 --> 39:28.889
[sighs softly]

573
39:29.764 --> 39:32.309
[Namgung] I told my landlord I'm not renewing the lease.

574
39:32.851 --> 39:34.352
I'll move out in a month,

575
39:35.812 --> 39:36.897
and I won't…

576
39:39.941 --> 39:41.860
see you ever again after tomorrow.

577
39:43.153 --> 39:44.237
Hey, Namgung…

578
39:45.488 --> 39:46.323
Mi-do…

579
39:49.743 --> 39:50.869
let's take a holiday.

580
39:55.457 --> 39:58.001
There's a place I really want to visit with you.

581
40:00.253 --> 40:01.796
[soft, somber music playing]

582
40:17.520 --> 40:19.189
[Namgung] Tomorrow, Gangnam Bus Terminal,

583
40:19.522 --> 40:21.399
Platform 13 at 9:10 a.m.

584
40:22.734 --> 40:24.444
Don't come if you don't want to,

585
40:24.569 --> 40:29.950
but if you don't, this will be the last time we see each other.

586
40:37.582 --> 40:38.875
[gentle, somber music concludes]

587
40:39.000 --> 40:40.794
[cutesy alarm ringing]

588
40:52.430 --> 40:53.306
[alarm stops]

589
41:37.851 --> 41:40.729
[seabirds calling]

590
41:49.446 --> 41:50.363
[sighs]

591
41:52.073 --> 41:52.949
Mi-do…

592
41:54.784 --> 41:56.077
let's make a promise today.

593
41:57.620 --> 42:00.999
Just for today, let's be completely honest, no lies.

594
42:03.001 --> 42:06.671
If either of us lies, forehead flick, deal?

595
42:09.632 --> 42:11.676
Sorry, but I've always been honest with you.

596
42:14.095 --> 42:16.139
Why do you feel the need to say that?

597
42:19.642 --> 42:22.562
Did you go to Damyang with Gong Ji-seok on my discharge day?

598
42:28.026 --> 42:28.860
No.

599
42:29.569 --> 42:31.404
I didn't. I had a field trip for my grad--

600
42:31.529 --> 42:32.530
Ah!

601
42:33.782 --> 42:36.242
[breathes deeply]

602
42:39.662 --> 42:40.497
What about you?

603
42:41.039 --> 42:42.540
Where were you when I turned 22?

604
42:43.583 --> 42:44.834
After I dumped you?

605
42:46.211 --> 42:48.171
You went to Cho Angela's, didn't you?

606
42:48.296 --> 42:49.506
I went to a motel.

607
42:50.882 --> 42:51.966
We both went.

608
42:54.719 --> 42:56.679
You sound just really proud of that.

609
42:56.805 --> 42:58.431
We weren't dating back then,

610
42:58.556 --> 43:00.392
and I dated Cho Angela after that day.

611
43:00.517 --> 43:01.601
What's the big deal?

612
43:09.692 --> 43:10.819
You regret knowing me?

613
43:12.278 --> 43:14.406
Do you regret having me in your life?

614
43:21.413 --> 43:22.247
No.

615
43:22.831 --> 43:25.333
I've never regretted knowing you for a single second.

616
43:27.877 --> 43:29.671
Because that day was an accident.

617
43:31.423 --> 43:33.383
It was truly an unavoidable accident.

618
43:35.135 --> 43:35.969
What about you?

619
43:36.803 --> 43:37.637
You regret knowing me?

620
43:37.887 --> 43:38.847
Yes, I do.

621
43:40.640 --> 43:42.600
-[somber music playing] -[Namgung] I thought I was a curse

622
43:43.101 --> 43:45.645
who brought the worst things into your life, Mi-do.

623
43:45.770 --> 43:46.646
Namgung…

624
43:47.063 --> 43:49.899
If you and I had met like ordinary people…

625
43:51.985 --> 43:53.695
our ending would have been different.

626
43:55.280 --> 43:56.364
It makes me bitter.

627
44:06.416 --> 44:07.959
So that's why you brought me here.

628
44:08.793 --> 44:10.336
To say everything you wanted to say.

629
44:10.837 --> 44:12.464
Hear everything you needed to.

630
44:13.339 --> 44:14.466
And leave nothing behind.

631
44:16.968 --> 44:18.511
You won't see me after today?

632
44:20.763 --> 44:21.806
Okay.

633
44:22.265 --> 44:23.099
Let's do it.

634
44:24.392 --> 44:26.102
Let's say goodbye here and now.

635
44:27.103 --> 44:27.937
Good luck.

636
44:38.615 --> 44:42.035
VACANT

637
44:42.160 --> 44:43.703
GANGNEUNG, BEAUTIFUL ALL YEAR

638
44:43.828 --> 44:45.163
[Mi-do] To the terminal, sir.

639
45:00.803 --> 45:02.305
You came back earlier than I thought.

640
45:04.807 --> 45:06.559
I thought you'd be another hour.

641
45:08.394 --> 45:09.229
Let's go.

642
45:09.729 --> 45:11.439
There's a gift I want from you.

643
45:19.489 --> 45:21.324
Mi-do the weirdo.

644
45:21.741 --> 45:22.784
Mi-do the dork.

645
45:23.284 --> 45:24.494
[trills tongue]

646
45:26.079 --> 45:27.038
Come on, smile.

647
45:29.249 --> 45:31.000
It's our last time. At least smile.

648
45:31.501 --> 45:32.418
[sighs]

649
45:36.381 --> 45:41.302
Like I have always said, you look beautiful when you smile.

650
45:48.434 --> 45:49.269
Are you hungry?

651
45:50.436 --> 45:51.521
You barely ate earlier.

652
45:51.896 --> 45:53.147
Just tell me what it is you want.

653
45:53.690 --> 45:54.649
I'll buy it and just leave.

654
45:55.066 --> 45:56.693
Come on, it's our last day anyway.

655
45:56.818 --> 45:58.111
Stay with me until midnight.

656
45:58.236 --> 45:59.404
-Mi-do! -Hey!

657
46:00.989 --> 46:03.908
[breathing heavily]

658
46:10.415 --> 46:12.333
Um, balloon.

659
46:16.045 --> 46:18.339
The dinosaur balloon you gave me when we first met.

660
46:21.593 --> 46:22.885
I want one just like that.

661
46:26.306 --> 46:27.807
Actually, that balloon…

662
46:29.767 --> 46:31.644
was the first gift I ever got.

663
46:35.607 --> 46:39.110
So when I lost it, I was really sad.

664
46:50.538 --> 46:51.664
That was 20 years ago.

665
46:52.123 --> 46:53.708
They wouldn't have the same one.

666
46:54.250 --> 46:55.251
Seriously?

667
46:55.501 --> 46:57.629
Who would sell old-fashioned balloons these days?

668
46:59.255 --> 47:02.175
-[toy squeaking] -[light, mid-tempo music playing]

669
47:29.619 --> 47:31.329
[exhales deeply]

670
47:40.838 --> 47:41.881
[teenager 1] Rock, paper, scissors!

671
47:42.006 --> 47:43.007
Hey, hey, hey.

672
47:43.132 --> 47:44.425
[teenagers] Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

673
47:45.093 --> 47:46.719
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

674
47:46.844 --> 47:48.054
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

675
47:48.179 --> 47:49.138
Oh, no!

676
47:49.263 --> 47:50.223
[teenager 1] Oh, no!

677
47:50.348 --> 47:51.474
You okay?

678
47:51.933 --> 47:52.767
Are you okay?

679
47:53.351 --> 47:55.144
-Thank you. -[Namgung chuckles] Be careful.

680
47:55.269 --> 47:56.104
[father] Say thank you.

681
47:56.437 --> 47:57.271
You okay?

682
47:59.899 --> 48:01.192
[teenager 2] Excuse me!

683
48:01.859 --> 48:03.903
-Could you take our picture? Please? -[Namgung] Oh, sure.

684
48:04.362 --> 48:05.571
-Visiting? -[teenager 2] Yeah.

685
48:06.030 --> 48:07.156
[Namgung] All right, get together.

686
48:07.824 --> 48:09.117
One, two, three.

687
48:09.242 --> 48:10.243
[phone camera clicks]

688
48:10.368 --> 48:12.078
[Namgung] Guys, now jump on three.

689
48:12.203 --> 48:13.538
[teenagers chattering excitedly]

690
48:13.663 --> 48:15.081
[Namgung] One, two, three.

691
48:15.206 --> 48:16.457
[grunting]

692
48:16.582 --> 48:18.000
-[laughing] -Did you get it?

693
48:18.584 --> 48:21.003
-[Namgung] Do you wanna take a look? -[teenager 3] Yeah, it's okay.

694
48:21.129 --> 48:22.338
[teenager 2] Oh, thank you!

695
48:22.463 --> 48:23.756
[teenager 3] Thank you so much!

696
48:23.881 --> 48:25.341
[teenager 4] Really appreciate it!

697
48:28.636 --> 48:29.971
[light, mid-tempo music concludes]

698
48:30.096 --> 48:31.305
That's my balloon.

699
48:34.392 --> 48:35.226
Hey!

700
48:35.601 --> 48:36.811
I'll give you one next year.

701
48:38.730 --> 48:40.148
We don't have to come to Gangneung.

702
48:40.982 --> 48:42.442
I'll just buy you one next year.

703
48:44.986 --> 48:47.697
You said you'd see Yeong-do and Wan-do once a year.

704
48:48.823 --> 48:50.199
You don't have to see me that often,

705
48:50.324 --> 48:51.325
so just…

706
48:52.452 --> 48:53.828
don't say today is the end,

707
48:54.203 --> 48:56.289
or that you'll never see me again. Come on!

708
48:59.000 --> 49:00.835
[emotional music playing]

709
49:06.841 --> 49:08.468
Mi-do, do you want to know a secret?

710
49:12.930 --> 49:16.601
Actually, I won't see Yeong-do and Wan-do.

711
49:19.228 --> 49:21.272
They need some time to process this.

712
49:24.233 --> 49:25.735
So I'm just waiting for them to do it.

713
49:28.321 --> 49:29.447
Every three years

714
49:31.282 --> 49:32.325
and every five years.

715
49:34.368 --> 49:35.453
That's how I'll fade away.

716
49:38.414 --> 49:40.958
Namgung, don't do this.

717
49:41.083 --> 49:42.418
Why? Why?

718
49:42.960 --> 49:43.836
Mi-do.

719
49:47.548 --> 49:49.509
Why did you give me that balloon?

720
49:50.301 --> 49:52.595
[breathing heavily]

721
49:53.387 --> 49:55.014
I always wondered that.

722
49:59.769 --> 50:01.145
Why did you give it to me?

723
50:04.065 --> 50:05.399
Did you feel sorry for me?

724
50:13.616 --> 50:14.617
I won't tell you.

725
50:16.327 --> 50:17.829
You said you'd never see me again.

726
50:18.663 --> 50:20.456
Then I'm never telling you either.

727
50:23.167 --> 50:25.419
[sobbing]

728
50:37.056 --> 50:40.059
[sobbing]

729
51:15.303 --> 51:16.679
[emotional music concludes]

730
51:16.804 --> 51:19.390
[beach-goers chatting indistinctly]

731
51:24.353 --> 51:25.605
[man 1] Somebody get someone!

732
51:25.730 --> 51:26.856
[beach-goers clamoring]

733
51:26.981 --> 51:28.024
[woman 1] Oh, my God!

734
51:28.149 --> 51:29.567
[teenager 1] Somebody help him!

735
51:30.693 --> 51:31.569
[man 1] Please, someone!

736
51:31.694 --> 51:33.863
-[woman 2] Is he drowning? -[man 1] Someone help!

737
51:33.988 --> 51:35.781
[teenager 2] Somebody help! Somebody help, please!

738
51:35.907 --> 51:38.034
-[teenager 1] Somebody help! -[teenager 2] We need to call someone.

739
51:38.159 --> 51:39.410
[man 1] Someone help them!

740
51:39.535 --> 51:41.454
[tense, somber music playing]

741
51:41.579 --> 51:42.872
[woman 3] Should we help her?

742
51:43.456 --> 51:44.832
[man 1] You got it! You got it!

743
51:46.250 --> 51:48.294
You got it! Come on!

744
51:48.419 --> 51:49.295
[pants]

745
51:51.422 --> 51:52.673
[man 1] You got it, come on!

746
51:52.798 --> 51:54.342
[teenager 3 straining]

747
52:00.139 --> 52:01.307
No!

748
52:09.607 --> 52:12.026
[panting heavily]

749
52:17.698 --> 52:18.532
Thank you.

750
52:18.658 --> 52:20.242
-Thank you. -Thank you.

751
52:21.160 --> 52:22.328
-Thank you. -You okay?

752
52:28.751 --> 52:29.585
Hey.

753
52:29.710 --> 52:31.003
Don't be mad.

754
52:33.005 --> 52:33.839
You can't be mad.

755
52:33.965 --> 52:34.924
It's our last time.

756
52:39.720 --> 52:40.554
Namgung.

757
52:42.932 --> 52:43.933
You're so wrong.

758
52:47.937 --> 52:49.105
How is this a curse?

759
52:50.856 --> 52:52.149
[tense, somber music concludes]

760
52:52.274 --> 52:54.276
I was scared the whole time I was running.

761
52:56.570 --> 52:58.197
But I couldn't stop at all.

762
53:02.743 --> 53:03.661
You were too.

763
53:08.541 --> 53:10.209
My father would have felt like that.

764
53:28.936 --> 53:30.021
It's not a curse.

765
53:32.356 --> 53:33.190
It's a miracle.

766
53:37.778 --> 53:39.488
It was a miracle that we met.

767
53:44.243 --> 53:45.077
Still, Namgung…

768
53:47.371 --> 53:48.706
if your surviving…

769
53:50.875 --> 53:54.128
turns into regret and self-blame…

770
53:56.172 --> 53:58.049
and it feels like this is all a curse…

771
54:01.177 --> 54:03.262
remember that kid you and I saved.

772
54:07.850 --> 54:09.518
That alone makes our knowing each other

773
54:09.643 --> 54:11.645
more than enough of a blessing, I think.

774
54:11.771 --> 54:13.689
[tender music playing]

775
54:16.859 --> 54:18.527
[sobbing softly]

776
54:27.578 --> 54:29.038
I wanted you to be happy.

777
54:33.375 --> 54:34.752
When I gave you that balloon…

778
54:37.296 --> 54:41.133
I just hoped that little boy would be really happy, you know?

779
54:41.759 --> 54:42.968
That's what I thought.

780
54:46.305 --> 54:47.473
I was happy.

781
54:50.184 --> 54:56.649
Mi-do, I have been really happy since the very first moment I met you.

782
54:58.526 --> 55:02.363
You're the one who taught me that life could be this happy.

783
55:03.447 --> 55:04.490
That's what kept me alive.

784
55:04.615 --> 55:06.450
That's how I carried on.

785
55:07.243 --> 55:09.245
I was able to try my hardest to live.

786
55:19.463 --> 55:21.757
What about you, Mi-do?

787
55:23.134 --> 55:24.969
Are you really happy with me?

788
55:36.605 --> 55:39.150
It was worth giving my all to this, Namgung.

789
55:42.236 --> 55:45.072
So happy I was with you.

790
56:04.175 --> 56:05.342
[teenager] Excuse me.

791
56:05.968 --> 56:08.304
This was caught on a shop sign over there.

792
56:12.141 --> 56:13.851
Again, thank you so much.

793
56:22.234 --> 56:23.611
[chuckles]

794
56:49.970 --> 56:51.263
[tender music concludes]

795
57:10.115 --> 57:11.408
We have eight minutes left.

796
57:14.662 --> 57:17.414
If you have any last questions, ask away.

797
57:18.332 --> 57:20.584
What did you do with Angela at the motel, huh?

798
57:26.757 --> 57:27.591
Forget it.

799
57:27.716 --> 57:28.550
Don't tell me.

800
57:29.134 --> 57:30.302
I don't want to know.

801
57:30.427 --> 57:31.595
[laughs]

802
57:38.978 --> 57:39.812
Mi-do.

803
57:42.856 --> 57:43.691
Mmm?

804
57:46.318 --> 57:47.403
Lee Mi-do.

805
57:49.321 --> 57:50.155
Mmm?

806
57:53.909 --> 57:55.744
Can you please say my name again?

807
57:58.789 --> 58:00.749
[sweet, sentimental music playing]

808
58:08.007 --> 58:09.091
Namgung Ho.

809
58:14.430 --> 58:17.141
A happy sucker, Namgung Ho.

810
58:17.266 --> 58:19.101
[laughs]

811
58:21.270 --> 58:22.271
[laughs]

812
58:45.210 --> 58:46.837
[sighs deeply]

813
59:04.772 --> 59:06.774
[sweet, sentimental music concludes]

814
59:08.901 --> 59:10.361
[Ms. Ma] I totally got ripped off.

815
59:10.486 --> 59:11.487
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

816
59:11.612 --> 59:13.155
A hundred thousand won each.

817
59:14.239 --> 59:16.367
Not even a discount, those assholes.

818
59:17.201 --> 59:18.035
Listen to me,

819
59:18.160 --> 59:20.120
quitting movies is one thing, Mi-do.

820
59:21.205 --> 59:22.831
But that doesn't erase your past.

821
59:22.956 --> 59:24.666
Nothing in this world can erase it.

822
59:26.627 --> 59:30.381
All that time you worked hard and gave your all, that's yours.

823
59:31.173 --> 59:32.007
So…

824
59:34.093 --> 59:35.052
[sighs]

825
59:35.886 --> 59:38.055
…don't you tear it or ruin it, hmm?

826
59:38.806 --> 59:40.182
You have to cherish it.

827
59:41.850 --> 59:44.520
Both the movie and Hoya.

828
59:46.146 --> 59:47.439
You must cherish that.

829
59:58.951 --> 59:59.785
[Yeong-do] What?

830
01:00:00.285 --> 01:00:01.286
Why are you here?

831
01:00:01.912 --> 01:00:02.913
[Tae-seung] Came to see Mi-do.

832
01:00:03.872 --> 01:00:04.790
I'm dating Mi-do.

833
01:00:05.374 --> 01:00:07.584
[Yeong-do] Huh? Hey, I won't be your brother-in-law.

834
01:00:08.794 --> 01:00:09.628
Get lost.

835
01:00:10.504 --> 01:00:13.006
[Tae-seung] Same here. I don't want you as a brother either.

836
01:00:13.132 --> 01:00:14.425
Look at that idiot.

837
01:00:14.550 --> 01:00:16.343
He's back again. What does he want?

838
01:00:16.885 --> 01:00:18.720
[Tae-seung] Why don't you come and talk down to me, pal?

839
01:00:18.846 --> 01:00:19.680
[Yeong-do] What?

840
01:00:19.805 --> 01:00:20.973
Pal? [scoffs]

841
01:00:21.640 --> 01:00:22.766
What did you say? "Pal"?

842
01:00:23.100 --> 01:00:24.059
I'm older!

843
01:00:24.393 --> 01:00:25.227
My face looks older.

844
01:00:25.352 --> 01:00:26.937
[Tae-seung] Hey, hey, hey, let go of my collar.

845
01:00:27.062 --> 01:00:29.314
-[Yeong-do] Oh! Oh! Fighting back? -[Tae-seung] Hitting me again?

846
01:00:59.887 --> 01:01:01.930
[Wan-do] Namgung found something of yours while packing.

847
01:01:02.890 --> 01:01:03.974
He left it by your door.

848
01:01:04.349 --> 01:01:05.392
Did you see it?

849
01:01:09.771 --> 01:01:11.106
[soft, tender music playing]

850
01:01:20.240 --> 01:01:25.871
[Mi-do] Namgung, I gave you and you gave me a seed.

851
01:01:31.919 --> 01:01:35.088
Namgung, you have received seeds

852
01:01:35.214 --> 01:01:37.591
from so many people during your life.

853
01:01:38.926 --> 01:01:41.261
Your biological father who left you at birth.

854
01:01:42.763 --> 01:01:44.473
My dad who died saving you.

855
01:01:45.891 --> 01:01:48.352
Aunt Hwa-young who broke you again and again.

856
01:01:49.019 --> 01:01:50.604
Art, once your whole world.

857
01:01:52.147 --> 01:01:54.233
Ssuk, the cat I was jealous of.

858
01:01:55.275 --> 01:01:57.236
Sol, who was so much like you.

859
01:01:58.278 --> 01:02:00.864
So many people gave you seeds and then left.

860
01:02:16.421 --> 01:02:20.384
SLAM DUNK, VOL. 8

861
01:02:20.884 --> 01:02:25.389
[Mi-do] Namgung, you have given me such deep and unique love.

862
01:02:25.847 --> 01:02:28.767
And you have always looked at the world with such warmth.

863
01:02:31.645 --> 01:02:33.814
Because you didn't neglect any of those seeds.

864
01:02:34.690 --> 01:02:37.359
You made them grow strong and helped them bloom.

865
01:02:41.905 --> 01:02:45.284
So Namgung, just like you,

866
01:02:46.410 --> 01:02:49.496
I'm going to nurture this seed you gave me.

867
01:02:50.998 --> 01:02:52.457
Without neglecting it.

868
01:02:53.333 --> 01:02:55.252
Without letting it fester and rot.

869
01:02:56.044 --> 01:02:58.130
Without trampling and killing it.

870
01:02:59.006 --> 01:03:02.050
I'll nurture it warmly with the love you taught me.

871
01:03:03.302 --> 01:03:05.512
And I will make sure it blooms.

872
01:03:11.643 --> 01:03:12.853
[music swells]

873
01:03:22.321 --> 01:03:23.447
[Mi-do] Namgung,

874
01:03:24.239 --> 01:03:27.075
instead of the first snow, let's wait for spring now.

875
01:03:29.036 --> 01:03:32.289
The spring when the seeds you gave me blooms inside me.

876
01:03:34.374 --> 01:03:37.210
The spring when the seed I gave you blooms inside you.

877
01:03:40.464 --> 01:03:42.090
And let's love that spring…

878
01:03:44.092 --> 01:03:44.926
forever.

879
01:03:57.731 --> 01:03:59.524
[pencil scratching]

880
01:04:06.114 --> 01:04:08.075
[music rises]

881
01:05:03.547 --> 01:05:05.757
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

882
01:05:05.882 --> 01:05:07.259
[soft, tender music concludes]

883
01:05:07.384 --> 01:05:08.969
["Stay" playing]

884
01:05:19.438 --> 01:05:20.605
THANK YOU TO KIM YOON-HYE FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

885
01:05:51.344 --> 01:05:54.306
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

886
01:05:59.311 --> 01:06:00.395
[song concludes]
